    {
      "block_id": "2605.06070_p4_b32",
      "text": "Figure 3: Overview of the proposed ArenaPO. First, we build a model Arena that converts image-\nlevel pairwise comparisons in the dataset into model-level comparisons, and updates each model\u2019s\ncapability distribution using Bayesian inference. Second, for each data instance, the two images\nare regarded as samples from their corresponding capability distributions. Conditioned on the two\ndistributions and the observed binary preference, we estimate the quality gap using latent-variable\ninference via truncated normal distribution. Finally, the estimated quality gap serves as an offline,\nfine-grained reward to enable more effective preference optimization.\n",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        312.18,
        505.65,
        387.67
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        432,
        1248,
        2022,
        1550
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 10.06,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 658,
      "block_type": 0
    },
